                <pb facs="0503" n="433" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg433"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">713.1311/242: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-02-15T12:00:00-05:45">February 15,
                        1934—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>49. My 47, February 10 [<hi rendition="#italic">13</hi>], 2 p.m. Press of this
                    morning publishes telegram from Guatemalan Minister for Foreign Affairs to
                    Nicaraguan Minister for Foreign Affairs offering the use of airplane to bring to
                    Guatemala on February 18 Nicaraguan delegates to Central American
                    Conference.</p>
                <p>Minister for Foreign Affairs has just informed me that this telegram crossed
                    telegram sent yesterday by President Sacasa to Presidents of other Central
                    American states proposing March 15th as date of Conference.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Central American missions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
